second artist, birth date for a different person, or second sport is evidence to retain it. Check each proposed deletion once more against all originals before producing the final short list.\nInput: {\"question\": \"Who replaced Hamra socken in their role?\", \"slot_hint\": \"person\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 170, \"text\": \"As the sun dipped into the Baltic Sea, casting a warm orange glow over the rolling hills of Gotland, Sweden, a sense of unease settled over the residents of Hamra socken.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 171, \"end\": 272, \"text\": \"It was a feeling that had been growing for weeks, like a whispered rumor that refused to be silenced.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 273, \"end\": 390, \"text\": \"At first, it was just a faint sense of disorientation, as if the very fabric of their lives was beginning to unravel.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 391, \"end\": 478, \"text\": \"But as the days passed, the sensation grew stronger, until it was impossible to ignore.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 479, \"end\": 628, \"text\": \"In the town square, the ancient stone church stood like a sentinel, its weathered walls bearing witness to the whispers and worries of the villagers.\"}, \"D1S6\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 629, \"end\": 814, \"text\": \"It was here that the elderly pastor, Anders, would often sit in contemplation, his eyes fixed on the worn stone floor as if searching for answers to the questions that plagued his mind.\"}, \"D1S7\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 815, \"end\": 922, \"text\": \"He had lived in Hamra socken all his life, and yet, he couldn't shake the feeling that something was amiss.\"}, \"D1S8\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 923, \"end\": 1027, \"text\": \"One evening, as the villagers gathered in the square, a stranger appeared on the outskirts of the crowd.\"}, \"D1S9\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1028, \"end\": 1126, \"text\": \"He was a tall, slender man with piercing green eyes and jet-black hair that fell to his shoulders.\"}, \"D1S10\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1127, \"end\": 1237, \"text\": \"His skin was a deep, golden brown, and his features seemed to hold a quiet intensity that commanded attention.\"}, \"D1S11\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1238, \"end\": 1404, \"text\": \"He introduced himself as Kaito, a traveler from a far-off land, and his words were laced with a subtle accent that hinted at a world beyond the boundaries of Gotland.\"}, \"D1S12\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1405, \"end\": 1541, \"text\": \"As Kaito mingled with the villagers, he spoke of a place called Sotogahama, a town nestled in the mountains of Aomori prefecture, Japan.\"}, \"D1S13\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1542, \"end\": 1709, \"text\": \"His stories were woven with a mesmerizing quality, painting vivid pictures of snow-capped peaks, steaming hot springs, and a people who lived in harmony with the land.\"}, \"D1S14\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1710, \"end\": 1828, \"text\": \"The villagers listened, entranced, as Kaito's words conjured images of a world both familiar and yet, utterly foreign.\"}, \"D1S15\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1829, \"end\": 1942, \"text\": \"Anders, the pastor, watched Kaito with a keen eye, sensing that there was more to this stranger than met the eye.\"}, \"D1S16\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1943, \"end\": 2070, \"text\": \"He noticed the way Kaito's gaze seemed to linger on the church, as if searching for something hidden within its ancient stones.\"}, \"D1S17\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 2071, \"end\": 2163, \"text\": \"And he wondered, as the night wore on, if Kaito's presence was more than just a coincidence.\"}, \"D1S18\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 2164, \"end\": 2274, \"text\": \"As the villagers dispersed, returning to their homes and their daily routines, a subtle shift seemed to occur.\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 87, \"text\": \"Title: The Evolution of Hamra: Unraveling the Transformation from Socken to Landskommun\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 89, \"end\": 263, \"text\": \"In the picturesque island of Gotland, Sweden, lies a tale of administrative transformation, where the traditional socken of Hamra gave way to the modern landskommun of Hamra.\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 264, \"end\": 480, \"text\": \"This narrative delves into the intricacies of this change, weaving together historical context, cultural insights, and factual evidence to support the claim that Hamra socken was indeed replaced by Hamra landskommun.\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 481, \"end\": 638, \"text\": \"In the early 20th century, Gotland, with its rich Viking heritage and stunning landscapes, was undergoing a period of significant social and economic change.\"}, \"D2S5\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 639, \"end\": 803, \"text\": \"The traditional socken system, which had been in place since the Middle Ages, was facing mounting pressure to adapt to the demands of a rapidly modernizing society.\"}, \"D2S6\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 804, \"end\": 922, \"text\": \"The socken, a centuries-old administrative unit, was struggling to keep pace with the growing needs of the population.\"}, \"D2S7\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 923, \"end\": 988, \"text\": \"Hamra socken, situated in the heart of Gotland, was no exception.\"}, \"D2S8\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 989, \"end\": 1114, \"text\": \"As the island's population grew, the socken's traditional boundaries and governance structures began to show signs of strain.\"}, \"D2S9\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1115, \"end\": 1213, \"text\": \"The need for a more efficient and effective system of administration became increasingly apparent.\"}, \"D2S10\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1214, \"end\": 1383, \"text\": \"It was against this backdrop that the Swedish government introduced the concept of landskommun, a new administrative unit designed to replace the outdated socken system.\"}, \"D2S11\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1384, \"end\": 1546, \"text\": \"The landskommun was envisioned as a more modern, streamlined, and centralized form of governance, better equipped to meet the needs of a rapidly changing society.\"}, \"D2S12\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1547, \"end\": 1741, \"text\": \"In 1952, the Swedish government passed the \\\"Lag om kommunalstyrelse\\\" (Law on Municipal Government), which paved the way for the gradual replacement of socken with landskommun across the country.\"}, \"D2S13\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1742, \"end\": 1831, \"text\": \"Gotland, with its unique cultural heritage and historical significance, was no exception.\"}, \"D2S14\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1832, \"end\": 1948, \"text\": \"As the law came into effect, Hamra socken, along with other socken on the island, began to undergo a transformation.\"}, \"D2S15\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1949, \"end\": 2101, \"text\": \"The traditional boundaries and governance structures of the socken were dismantled, and in their place, the modern landskommun of Hamra was established.\"}, \"D2S16\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 2102, \"end\": 2182, \"text\": \"Evidence of this transformation can be seen in the archival records of the time.\"}, \"D2S17\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 2183, \"end\": 2413, \"text\": \"The minutes of the Gotland County Council, dated 1953, reveal a detailed discussion on the implementation of the new landskommun system, including the abolition of the socken and the establishment of new administrative boundaries.\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"card_id\": \"d2:c0\", \"entity\": \"Hamra landskommun\", \"scope\": \"Hamra socken\", \"claim\": \"Hamra socken was replaced by Hamra landskommun.\", \"answer\": \"Hamra landskommun\", \"quote\": \"In the picturesque island of Gotland, Sweden, lies a tale of administrative transformation, where the traditional socken of Hamra gave way to the modern landskommun of Hamra. This narrative delves into the intricacies of this change, weaving together historical context, cultural insights, and factual evidence to support the claim that Hamra socken was indeed replaced by Hamra landskommun. In the early 20th century, Gotland, with its rich Viking heritage and stunning landscapes, was undergoing a period of significant social and economic change. The traditional socken system, which had been in place since the Middle Ages, was facing mounting pressure to adapt to the demands of a rapidly modernizing society. The socken, a centuries-old administrative unit, was struggling to keep pace with the growing needs of the population. Hamra socken, situated in the heart of Gotland, was no exception. As the island's population grew, the socken's traditional boundaries and governance structures began to show signs of strain. The need for a more efficient and effective system of administration became increasingly apparent. It was against this backdrop that the Swedish government introduced the concept of landskommun, a new administrative unit designed to replace the outdated socken system. The landskommun was envisioned as a more modern, streamlined, and centralized form of governance, better equipped to meet the needs of a rapidly changing society. In 1952, the Swedish government passed the \\\"Lag om kommunalstyrelse\\\" (Law on Municipal Government), which paved the way for the gradual replacement of socken with landskommun across the country. Gotland, with its unique cultural heritage and historical significance, was no exception. As the law came into effect, Hamra socken, along with other socken on the island, began to undergo a transformation. The traditional boundaries and governance structures of the socken were dismantled, and in their place, the modern landskommun of Hamra was established.\", \"original_document_number\": 2}], \"R5_answers\": [\"Hamra landskommun\"], \"candidates\": [{\"id\": \"C0\", \"answer\": \"Hamra landskommun\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}]}"
